@yxieca thanks for the review. 
1. Agreed, I have changed the command to use `logrotate -f /etc/logrotate.conf` instead of `logrotate --force /etc/logrotate.d/rsyslog` since it is far more standard in the codebase.
2. No action needed, this is the specific check and error message that we are handling. The idea is that my monit handler function should be extended as/if needed in the future but I am handling this specific case.
